# yotuvia-web — template. Copy-real values into `.env.local`
# (git-ignored, chmod 600) so real credentials are never committed here.
# Full registration walkthrough: docs/oauth-setup.md at the repo root.
#
# Vite bakes every VITE_* variable into the bundle at BUILD time. Restarting the
# dev server is enough in development; a production change requires a rebuild.
#
# These are PUBLIC client ids, not secrets: they identify the web origin to the
# provider. The BACKEND NEEDS NO OAUTH KEYS — it validates the token the browser
# already obtained by calling the provider directly, so there is no matching
# server-side client id/secret. Never put a provider client SECRET in this file.
#
# Leave a value empty to disable that provider: the buttons degrade to a
# disabled state with an explanation instead of opening a broken popup.

# Google — Cloud Console > APIs & Services > Credentials > OAuth client ID
# (application type: "Web application"). Add every origin the web app is served
# from under "Authorised JavaScript origins", e.g.:
#   http://localhost:5173
#   https://<your-web-domain>
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Facebook — App ID of a Facebook app with "Facebook Login" added. Configure the
# web origins under Facebook Login > Settings (Valid OAuth Redirect URIs /
# Allowed Domains for JavaScript SDK), e.g. http://localhost:5173.
VITE_FACEBOOK_APP_ID=
